# evidata environment (copy to apps/web/.env.local for local dev)

# --- AI provider -------------------------------------------------------------
# Without these, the app uses the deterministic FixtureProvider (scripted demo
# answers) — the default for dev and CI. To use a real OpenAI-compatible model,
# set AGENT_PROVIDER=openai and a key.
#
# AGENT_PROVIDER=openai
#
# DeepSeek (defaults shown — base URL + model are optional):
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
# AGENT_MODEL=deepseek-chat
#
# …or any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint (OpenAI, Together, local Ollama/vLLM):
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# AGENT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# AGENT_MAX_TOKENS=4096   # default; raise if detailed answers get truncated

# --- Credential vault --------------------------------------------------------
# Required to register database Connections AND BYO-key models (their API keys are
# encrypted at rest, AES-256-GCM). Without it those create/decrypt paths return a
# clear "not configured" error (503). Generate: `openssl rand -base64 32`.
#
# APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=<base64 of 32 random bytes>
# APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY_ID=k1        # optional; defaults to k1
# Rotation (alternative to the single key above):
# APP_ENCRYPTION_KEYS=[{"id":"k2","key":"<base64>"},{"id":"k1","key":"<base64>"}]
# APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY_ID=k2        # selects the active key for new writes

# --- Multi-model (BYO-key) ---------------------------------------------------
# The env AI provider above is the simple single-model default. For per-user,
# multi-model use, sign in and register models at /admin/models (each with its own
# key, encrypted via APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY); pick one per conversation. See
# docs/tech-spec/14-byo-key-multi-model.md.
